{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "label": "S4 \u2014 tutor screen (stage doc, referenced)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-14", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "label": "S4 \u2014 Tutor Screen (research doc)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d30", "label": "D30 \u2014 GET /api/v2/lessons/:id returns one response; item history excluded", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "Three round trips for one screen is three chances to half-load; item history is editing-history display data for S5, not the tutor's first paint."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d31", "label": "D31 \u2014 sessions capped at 20, cap reported via sessionCount", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "A heavy user's lesson could carry hundreds of rows; a cap the client cannot see is a cap that lies."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d32", "label": "D32 \u2014 withBearer gains a generic route-context parameter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "Next.js hands a dynamic route handler a second params argument the original wrapper dropped; string-surgery routing does not scale."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d33", "label": "D33 \u2014 pause reasons come from onDisconnect, never inferred", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "Native reports a typed disconnect reason where the browser reported nothing; AppState must be logged, never branched on."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d34", "label": "D34 \u2014 wire onAgentResponseCorrection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "Without it a barge-in stores the sentence the tutor would have finished; the post-call webhook's overwrite already silently failed for 47 days once."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d35", "label": "D35 \u2014 session journal on expo-sqlite/kv-store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "First-party, AsyncStorage-shaped API that tracks the SDK rather than a fourth-party module, with a path into the future SQLite mirror."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d36", "label": "D36 \u2014 drop sendUserActivity entirely", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "The agents have no idle timeout to defeat, and its DOM-event triggers don't exist on a voice-only native screen."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d37", "label": "D37 \u2014 keep combined useConversation; do not split hooks yet", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "Splitting is a measured optimization and transcript rendering performance has not been measured."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d38", "label": "D38 \u2014 exercise sendContextualUpdate as a gate item, not a code review item", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "Transport is proven in source and by the kickoff; server-side handling of a contextual update over WebRTC cannot be verified from source."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d39", "label": "D39 \u2014 Expo UI applied narrowly: RN owns layout and scrolling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "matchContents on the same axis as a scroll container silently stops scrolling; the transcript stays outside SwiftUI entirely."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d40", "label": "D40 \u2014 never hold the screen awake (drop useKeepAwake)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "S1 measured a locked native app does not end the session; the web's keep-awake code was an apology for a browser-only problem."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d41", "label": "D41 \u2014 a session may not outlive the screen", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "ConversationProvider mounts above the router and UIBackgroundModes:audio means iOS won't suspend the app, so navigating away leaves a live, billed, listening session with no UI."}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d42", "label": "D42 \u2014 screen fetches by route-param lesson id; one hard-coded id remains as navigation only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d43", "label": "D43 \u2014 keep S3's probe screen, move it to /probe", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md", "rationale": "It is the regression instrument for every SDK/LiveKit/iOS upgrade; deleting a working instrument to keep the router tidy is a bad trade."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s3_conversation_token", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s1_background_audio", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_12_expo_app_creation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_12_expo_build_plan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d30", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d31", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d32", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d33", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d34", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d35", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"source": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen", "target": "docs_2026_08_13_expo_s4_tutor_screen_d36", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "docs/2026-08-13-expo-s4-tutor-screen.md"}, {"sou